Add dosage and duration into the metadata file.

`PFAS_metadata_all.csv` / `ref_water_metadata.csv` store the label as `chemical.y`.
PFAS `SraRunTable.csv` has its own `chemical` and does **not** include water SRRs (those are in the ref SRA table).
`merge(..., all = TRUE)` therefore keeps water rows from `SRR_filtered` but fills SRA columns with `NA` — including `chemical`. The water label is in `chemical.y`.
```{r}
unique(metadata_PFAS_filtered$chemical)
unique(SRR_filtered$chemical.y)
```

```{r}
metadata_PFAS_filtered_joined <- merge(metadata_PFAS_filtered, SRR_filtered, by = "SRR", all = TRUE) %>%
  mutate(chemical = chemical.y) # this so that we only have one chemical col (will be used by DESeq)

